+## Two WhyNot Cut installs on one account
+
+For example a dev or try marketplace beside the real one, or 3.0 beside 2.2.1.
+
+- Each install keeps its own options record, `~/.whynot-cut/plugin-options.<marketplace>.json`, and its own
+  `plugin-root.<marketplace>.json`. Its SessionStart writes them, and its `reel` reads its own record first. A
+  `--plugin-dir` checkout counts as the marketplace `inline`.
+- The shared `plugin-options.json` and `plugin-root.json` hold the last session's values, for the installer and
+  for earlier releases. 2.2.1 reads only the shared files, so its options follow whichever session started last.
+- To keep a test or try install fully apart, set `WHYNOT_OPTIONS_FILE` and `WHYNOT_HOME` to its own folder. It then
+  reads and writes only that file.
+- `reel doctor` from a second engine home does not offer `--fix --all-clients` for a clients folder it did not set,
+  for example one from the shared preferences file. Set that install's own `clients_root` first.
+- Claude Code adds each enabled plugin's `bin/` to the END of `PATH`. In a session where another install's `bin/`
+  comes first (2.2.1's, or the other marketplace's), a bare `reel` runs that install.
+  - `reel --version` names the install that ran.
+  - `reel doctor` → `reel_command` lists every `reel` on PATH and flags a wrong one first.
+  - To fix it, disable the other install in `/plugin` and restart Claude Code. Or call this install's wrapper by its
+    full path: `"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/bin/reel"` in bash, `& "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/bin/reel.cmd"` in PowerShell.
+
